      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "DeltaPack.SyncSession<T>",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/DeltaPack.SyncSession-1.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">A stateful handle over a one-way state-sync session between two endpoints.</p>\n<p>\nEach endpoint holds a <xref href=\"DeltaPack.SyncSession%601\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> representing the current\nshared view of the peer's state. The sender calls <xref href=\"DeltaPack.SyncSession%601.Encode(%600)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> to\nproduce bytes; the receiver calls <xref href=\"DeltaPack.SyncSession%601.Decode(System.Byte%5b%5d)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> to apply them. Both\nsides converge on the same view as long as messages are delivered in order.\n</p>\n<p>\nThe class handles the \"first call is full encode, subsequent are diffs\"\ndistinction internally. It also ensures the sender's view always matches\nwhat the peer reconstructs — even when the user's <code>state</code> object has\nbeen mutated or reordered in ways that would break a raw\n<code>EncodeDiff</code> call.\n</p>\n<p>\nPrefer the generated <code>CreateSyncSession()</code> factory on each schema type:\n</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-csharp\">var session = GameState.CreateSyncSession();</code></pre>\n<p>\nThe delegate-taking constructor below is the lower-level entry point — useful\nwhen you need to pass custom encode/decode/clone callbacks, but most callers\nshould go through the factory.\n</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/DeltaPack.TrackedList-1.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/DeltaPack.TrackedList-1.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "DeltaPack.TrackedList<T>",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/DeltaPack.TrackedList-1.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">A <xref href=\"System.Collections.Generic.List%601\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>-compatible list that records per-index version numbers\non every mutation. Intended as a drop-in replacement for <xref href=\"System.Collections.Generic.List%601\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>\non serialized properties of <xref href=\"DeltaPack.DeltaPackTrackedAttribute\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> classes so\n<code>EncodeDiff</code> can skip unchanged-index comparisons.</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/DeltaPack.TrackedOrderedDict-2.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/DeltaPack.TrackedOrderedDict-2.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "DeltaPack.TrackedOrderedDict<TKey, TValue>",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/DeltaPack.TrackedOrderedDict-2.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">An insertion-order-preserving dictionary that records per-key version numbers\non mutations. Intended as a drop-in replacement for <xref href=\"DeltaPack.OrderedDict%602\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>\non serialized properties of <xref href=\"DeltaPack.DeltaPackTrackedAttribute\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> classes.\nTracks three separate maps: updated keys (<code>DirtyKeys</code>), newly inserted\nkeys (<code>CreatedKeys</code>), and removed keys (<code>DeletedKeys</code>) so\n<code>EncodeDiff</code> can emit only actual changes since the last snapshot.</p>\n"
    },
